{"requirements":[{"id":"account","requirement":"Create the appworker account on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The account was absent initially, then directly observed with UID/GID 1000, home /home/appworker, and shell /bin/bash. It remained present with correct home ownership after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-09549ea4eed5485e","cmd-e8d7f182a87a48cd","cmd-f0bc8afc131a4090"]},{"id":"login_limits","requirement":"Limit appworker login sessions to 8,192 open files and 256 processes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Root-owned limits configuration sets matching soft and hard nofile and nproc limits. PAM-managed appworker sessions directly showed 8,192 open files and 256 processes both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e8d7f182a87a48cd","cmd-00560de2a9074be2","cmd-987b811ebda84c48","cmd-f0bc8afc131a4090"]},{"id":"platform_preservation","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 24.04 and kernel 6.8.0-71-generic were unchanged across execution and restart. The implementation used the platform's existing account and PAM limits facilities, with package health remaining intact.","evidence_ids":["cmd-09549ea4eed5485e","cmd-f0bc8afc131a4090","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Account creation and limits-file creation were required task changes (cmd-e8d7f182a87a48cd). The reboot and temporary restart log were required for the provider-wide restart protocol (cmd-84b8a89d105146e2); the log did not remain after reboot. The intervening connection reset was expected during reboot and does not indicate a harmful mutation (cmd-b0522b1f095644b8). Final observations show no failed services, no damaged package state, and no material unexpected exposure or temporary-file residue. The restart protocol was complete: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered account, limits, system, and service state were directly observed and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e8d7f182a87a48cd","cmd-987b811ebda84c48","cmd-84b8a89d105146e2","cmd-b0522b1f095644b8","cmd-56b3ed07534649d4","cmd-f0bc8afc131a4090","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct pre-change, runtime, persistence, and lifecycle evidence. The appworker account exists, its PAM login sessions enforce the requested limits, the operating-system release and kernel remain unchanged, and the mandatory restart evidence is complete and coherent.","limitations":[]}
